    description: "FOUND 2026-09-23 by the fundamental concept audit of IoPrimitive.kind (dev d917e02282).\nWrite-up: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/concept-audit-io-primitive-kind_09232026.md\nInstruments + 21 surveys: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/kind_audit_09232026/\n\nTHE FIELD HAS NO DEFINITION, AND THE CATALOGUES STATE THREE, IN THEIR OWN WORDS:\n  R3 \"what the analyzer stamps\":  java.yaml:169 (\"Static methods, catalogued\n      method-kind ... java's analyzer stamps call_construct=method on every\n      selector-expression call\"), kotlin.yaml:156 (\"the analyzer emits them as\n      function-kind calls, so they are catalogued as functions\")\n  R2 \"owner named, no value receiver\": cpp.yaml:96 (\"Static member functions,\n      hence function-kind\"), scala.yaml:129 (companion factories, \"no value\n      receiver\"), python.yaml Path.cwd / datetime (INV-nular, INV-fugus),\n      test_associated_fn_kinds.py (\"A receiverless callee must not be catalogued\n      as a method\"), WI-komun (\"methods: means called on an instance whose type\n      must be known; a named global is resolved by NAME\")\n  R1 \"what the callee is\": rust.yaml:405 (\"catalogued as a method because that\n      is what it IS\"), and INV-pimir's statement (\"IoPrimitive.kind names the\n      construct of the DEFINITION\")\nScala holds two rules in one merged catalogue: its own Source.fromFile is R2,\nand the java.nio.file.Files statics it inherits via _CATALOG_PARENTS are R3.\n\nEVERY CONSUMER THAT BRANCHES ON IT NEEDS R2:\n  verify_claims method_starved_modules route 1 (joins to call_construct) and route 2\n  (function names = matchable without a stamp); io_boundary gate_named_entry (method\n  rows need receiver verification); the untyped-receiver disclosures (method rows are\n  \"reached through a receiver\"); io_boundary.py:1161, the INV-nizom arm (drops\n  function rows when the stamp is method and the slot is multi-candidate).\nAnd the starvation gate's own premise is false on the main path: with a definite\nmodule slot, `_qualified_rows` and the module filter never read kind at all.\n\nMEASURED CONSEQUENCES (arm A shipped vs arm B = rows with no value receiver\nre-kinded to function; nothing else differs):\n  - JS `process` classified-yet-starved on 6/9 JS-bearing repos (filed separately\n    as the INV-fugus family item).\n  - java: R3 is LOAD-BEARING through the INV-nizom join. Re-kinding statics loses\n    41 classifications (jedis 160->124, petclinic -3, gatling -2), because java emits\n    a multi-candidate slot for wildcard imports and stamps method on qualified statics.\n  - scala/kotlin: re-kinding drops untyped-receiver disclosures, and in sbt 76 of the\n    297 dropped are REAL Files./System./Instant. calls whose qualifier the analyzer\n    dropped (WI-kilap; explicit imports too), so the disclosure is their only signal.\n  - swift: 16 constructor rows are keyed methods and can never match (INV-gujoh\n    discussion).\n\nPROPOSED STATEMENT, NOT ADOPTED (two shipped rulings collide: WI-komun + INV-nular's\ntest say R2, INV-pimir's statement says R1; the owner decides): `methods:` iff the\ncallee's owner is supplied at the call site by a VALUE whose type must be inferred;\n`functions:` iff the owner is named at the call site (module, namespace, type,\ncompanion object, named global) or there is none; `attributes:` iff read, not called.\n\nSEQUENCING, MEASURED: the JVM re-kind waits on (a) the INV-nizom arm no longer reading\na `method` stamp as receiver evidence and (b) the kotlin/scala static-qualifier drop.\nSwift waits on boundary adjudication. JS process and python ctypes.cdll are\nunconstrained. WI-fazad (declare the enum) should carry whatever axiom is adopted."  # ce9d
    fields:  # ce9d
      statement: "A catalogue row's kind is a property of the primitive, stated one way in every catalogue: methods iff the callee's owner is supplied at the call site by a value whose type must be inferred; functions iff the owner is named at the call site or there is none; attributes iff read, not called. It never encodes what one analyzer stamps."  # ce9d
      root_cause: "No definition was ever written (WI-fazad: undeclared bounded enum), so each catalogue tuned kind to make its own analyzer's call_construct stamp pass the construct-x-kind joins (method_starved_modules route 1; the INV-nizom arm of lookup_with_module). The value therefore encodes the analyzer, not the primitive; java.yaml and kotlin.yaml say so in their notes."  # ce9d
